RSX_ENGINE_PASS_DUMP_ONLY=<hex offset> (diag); a gate alone starts the dump

RSX_ENGINE_PASS_DUMP_ONLY keeps only the passes that render into, or sample,
a surface at that RSX offset (and only those draws in draws.txt), and writes
no presents, so one surface can be followed for minutes. With
RSX_ENGINE_PASS_DUMP_GATE set, the gate file alone starts the capture; before,
the min-draws condition also started it at boot. Off by default: no change
without the variables. Used 2026-10-21 to show Tokyo Jungle's map-tag name
sheet (local 0x03B40000) is never a render target: its text comes from the
CPU font path, which led to the HLE cellFont (src/font_hle.cpp).

